            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199663161?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update of HTTP example considering the comments on the issue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Just trying to start on the Open Source world</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">NA</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #24442.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1584737710\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/24442\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/24442/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/24442\">#24442</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Any correction or tips I'm glad to :D</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40096",
            "title": "Correction of HTTP example",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-02T19:43:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-26T21:37:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "santiagoOrozco-encora",
                "url": "https://github.com/santiagoOrozco-encora"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 128 adds support for a new <code class=\"notranslate\">hints</code> option that can be specified inside the <code class=\"notranslate\">publicKey</code> option of a Webauthn <code class=\"notranslate\">create()</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">get()</code> call, to hint to the browser what UI to show to the user for creating or authenticating with a security key. For example, do their users tend to use a physical security key like a YubiKey, or a smartphone-based authenticator app?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">hints</code> option was already covered on both the <code class=\"notranslate\">PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptions</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">PublicKeyCredentialRequestOptions</code> dictionary reference pages. This PR expands and improves on the provided information.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40091",
            "title": "Technical review: Update information on the Webauthn hints option",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-02T18:17:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-26T11:21:11.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4206148?u=9781d69322c4bb5003b5207f13eaa7316c3ec2fb&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mention that <code class=\"notranslate\">canvas</code> needs <code class=\"notranslate\">aria-label</code> rather than <code class=\"notranslate\">alt</code>, and mention the use of <code class=\"notranslate\">alt=\"\"</code> to signal that an image is purely decorative.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm new to <code class=\"notranslate\">canvas</code> and was confused when  the accessibility checker complained but the linked section only mentioned <code class=\"notranslate\">alt</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The existing text mentions that a label is needed for contentful images, but doesn't say how to stop the checker complaining for images that aren't contentful.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40089",
            "title": "Additions to \"Content with images must be labelled\"",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-26T01:47:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-26T01:43:03.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "mrec",
                "url": "https://github.com/mrec"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136 adds support to the MediaRecorder API for HEVC encoding, introducing the hvc1.* codec string, and adds new codecs (hev1.* and avc3.*) supporting variable resolution video in MP4. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6375884229181440\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6375884229181440</a> for more details.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR attempts to add some information about the new codecs to the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Media/Guides/Formats/codecs_parameter\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Media/Guides/Formats/codecs_parameter</a> page. The relevant MediaRecorder features all point to this page for the actual codec details, but to make sure the support is clear, I've also added compat data entries for them: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3175897756\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27142\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27142/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27142\">mdn/browser-compat-data#27142</a>.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40081",
            "title": "Technical review: Add information on missing MP4/HEVC codec parameter values",
